[HEADING=1]md2bbcode[/HEADING]
[B]A wrapper and plugin for [URL=https://github.com/lepture/mistune]Mistune[/URL].[/B] It converts most GitHub-flavored Markdown to Xenforo-flavored BBCode.
[ADMONITION=tip]Custom BBCodes made for RedGuides are included in [ICODE]bb_codes.xml[/ICODE], import the ones you want in your Xenforo installation at [ICODE]admin.php?bb-codes[/ICODE]. Some custom BBCodes include css, which you can split off to your extra.css template for more efficiency.[/ADMONITION]
[ADMONITION=note]This project is made with LLM assistance (derogatory).[/ADMONITION]
[HEADING=2]Installation[/HEADING]
Install as a CLI tool with [URL=https://pipx.pypa.io]pipx[/URL]:
[CODE=bash]pipx install md2bbcode
[/CODE]
[HEADING=2]Usage[/HEADING]
After installation, you can use md2bbcode from the command line:
[CODE=bash]md2bbcode README.md
[/CODE]
Output prints to stdout as UTF-8. To write straight to a file (recommended on Windows, where shell > redirection can mangle the encoding), use [ICODE]-o[/ICODE]:
[CODE=bash]md2bbcode README.md -o output.bbcode
[/CODE]
If the markdown includes relative images or other assets, you can use the --domain flag to prepend a domain to the relative URLs:
[CODE=bash]md2bbcode README.md --domain https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RedGuides/md2bbcode/main/
[/CODE]
You can also use the package in your Python project:
[CODE=python]from md2bbcode import process_readme

bbcode = process_readme("# Hell World")
print(bbcode)
[/CODE]
Pass a [ICODE]domain[/ICODE] to rewrite relative URLs (e.g. images and links in a repo README) to absolute ones:
[CODE=python]bbcode = process_readme(
    markdown_text,
    domain="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yourusername/yourrepo/main/",
)
[/CODE]
[HEADING=3]Debug Mode[/HEADING]
You can use the [ICODE]--debug[/ICODE] flag to save intermediate results to files for debugging:
[CODE=bash]md2bbcode README.md --debug
[/CODE]
[HEADING=2]Development[/HEADING]
If you want to contribute to md2bbcode or set up a development environment, follow these steps:
[LIST=1][*]Clone the repository:
[CODE=bash]git clone https://github.com/RedGuides/md2bbcode.git
cd md2bbcode
[/CODE]
[*]Create a development environment and install dependencies:
[CODE=bash]hatch env create
[/CODE]
[*]Activate the development environment:
[CODE=bash]hatch shell
[/CODE]
[/LIST]
[HEADING=3]renderers/bbcode.py[/HEADING]
The custom plugin for Mistune, which converts AST to bbcode.[SUP][U][JUMPTO=fn-1]1[/JUMPTO][/U][/SUP]
[HEADING=2]Additional Tools[/HEADING]
[HEADING=3]html2bbcode[/HEADING]
Converts most HTML tags typically allowed in Github Flavored Markdown to BBCode.[SUP][U][JUMPTO=fn-2]2[/JUMPTO][/U][/SUP]
[CODE=bash]html2bbcode input_file.html
[/CODE]
[HEADING=3]md2ast[/HEADING]
For debugging Mistune's renderer, converts a Markdown file to AST (JSON format).
[CODE=bash]md2ast input.md output.json
[/CODE]
[HEADING=2]Features Test[/HEADING]
Here are a few GitHub-flavored Markdown features so you can use this README.md for testing, including the table:
[TABLE]
[TR]
[TH][LEFT]Feature[/LEFT][/TH]
[TH][CENTER]Markdown[/CENTER][/TH]
[TH][RIGHT]Rendered[/RIGHT][/TH]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][LEFT]Bold[/LEFT][/TD]
[TD][CENTER][ICODE]**text**[/ICODE][/CENTER][/TD]
[TD][RIGHT][B]bold[/B][/RIGHT][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][LEFT]Italic[/LEFT][/TD]
[TD][CENTER][ICODE]*text*[/ICODE][/CENTER][/TD]
[TD][RIGHT][I]italic[/I][/RIGHT][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][LEFT]Strikethrough[/LEFT][/TD]
[TD][CENTER][ICODE]~~text~~[/ICODE][/CENTER][/TD]
[TD][RIGHT][S]struck[/S][/RIGHT][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][LEFT]Code[/LEFT][/TD]
[TD][CENTER][ICODE]`code`[/ICODE][/CENTER][/TD]
[TD][RIGHT][ICODE]inline[/ICODE][/RIGHT][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][LEFT]Link[/LEFT][/TD]
[TD][CENTER][ICODE][text](url)[/ICODE][/CENTER][/TD]
[TD][RIGHT][URL=https://example.com]example[/URL][/RIGHT][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][LEFT]Superscript[/LEFT][/TD]
[TD][CENTER][ICODE]<sup>2</sup>[/ICODE][/CENTER][/TD]
[TD][RIGHT]E=mc[SUP]2[/SUP][/RIGHT][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][LEFT]Subscript[/LEFT][/TD]
[TD][CENTER][ICODE]<sub>2</sub>[/ICODE][/CENTER][/TD]
[TD][RIGHT]H[SUB]2[/SUB]O[/RIGHT][/TD]
[/TR]
[/TABLE]
